# DOWN held through tab transitions (folder Long): R switches to the NOR
# list and L back while DOWN stays held. The SD list's glide brakes as the
# screen goes, and the list that comes back glides on at the held key's
# speed, its cursor on screen (the SD list comes back at its first row, as
# L from the NOR list always has). Every frame is hashed.
-w "screen ready: sd-list"
-k @8:DOWN -k @12:- -k @16:DOWN -k @20:-
-k @28:A -k @32:-
-w "screen ready: sd-list"
-k @8:DOWN
-k @110:DOWN+R -k @114:DOWN
-H @8:@300
-s @108:before.png
-s @118:going.png
-w "screen ready: nor-list"
-k @10:DOWN+L -k @14:DOWN
-s @30:back.png
-s @80:gliding.png
-k @120:-
-s @150:rest.png
